"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nHaving seen this spot mentioned in countless Australia travel blogs as a famous nighttime viewpoint, we timed our visit to arrive right as the sun was setting.  \n\nWhen we arrived after a leisurely walk, many people had already claimed their spots and were busy taking photos.  \nWe laid down a mat, found our spot, and waited for the sun to set.  \nThe wind was fairly strong, but fortunately it wasn't too cold.  \n\nBefore we knew it, while we were zoning out, the sun had gone down, and the night view was as stunning as rumored.  \nSydney Harbour Bridge looked spectacular, and in the distance we could also spot Luna Park Sydney with its somewhat unsettling entrance designed like a giant clown face.  \n\nWe zoned out a little longer before moving on to find somewhere for dinner.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"